+### Docker actions
+
+Six actions run the [Docker](Docker) tab's jobs, through the same
+`app.services.docker_actions` functions as its buttons. Machines without
+a confirmed host key or without Docker access are skipped; on each
+machine the jobs run one after another.
+
+| Action | Parameters |
+|---|---|
+| **Update Docker containers** (`docker_update`) | *Containers*: those set to update automatically (default), those the image check found a newer image for, or every container. *Vulnerability gate*: as set for each container (default), don't check, stop on a critical, on a critical or high, or when worse than the running image |
+| **Scan Docker images** (`docker_scan`) | *Images*: those containers use (default), those not scanned yet, or every image |
+| **Clean up Docker** (`docker_prune`) ⚠ | *Also remove*: nothing more (default — stopped containers, untagged images, unused networks, build cache), every image no container uses, or unused anonymous volumes. Named volumes are never removed by a schedule |
+| **Docker backup** (`docker_backup`) | — runs every backup marked *Run on schedule* |
+| **Check Docker backups** (`docker_backup_check`) | — `restic check` of each of them |
+| **Prune Docker backups** (`docker_backup_prune`) ⚠ | — `restic forget --prune` of each of them that has a retention; the rest are skipped |
+
+*Update automatically* on a container only means "picked by an *Update
+Docker containers* task with the first scope" — without such a task
+nothing updates on its own.
